module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjGlue.Basic

/-!
# Relative Proj over an arbitrary inclusion of affine opens

The relative homogeneous spectrum `Proj_S(𝒜)` of a quasi-coherent graded algebra is glued in
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjGlue.Basic` from the charts `Proj Γ(U, 𝒜)` indexed
by the *small affine Zariski site* of `S`, whose arrows are the **basic open** inclusions. Tags
01NO, 01NP and 01NQ quantify instead over an **arbitrary** inclusion of affine opens, so every
statement about a transition morphism has to be reproved at that generality. This file does that.

The one piece of real mathematics is the first statement below; everything after it is formal.

## Main results

* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjGeneral.irrelevant_le_map_res_of_le_opens`: **Tag 01N2
  for an arbitrary inclusion of affine opens.** For affine opens `U ⊆ V` of the base, the
  irrelevant ideal of `Γ(U, 𝒜)` is contained in the image of the irrelevant ideal of `Γ(V, 𝒜)`.
  This is Mathlib's own hypothesis for `AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.map`, so it unlocks the whole of
  that API at once.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjGeneral.mapDomain_res_eq_top_of_le_opens`: hence the
  morphism of projective spectra induced by restriction is defined everywhere — Tag 01NO's
  everywhere-defined morphism, for an arbitrary inclusion.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjGeneral.transition_comp_of_le_opens`: hence Tag 01NP, the
  transitivity of the transitions, at that generality.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjGeneral.transition_comp_chart_of_le_opens`: the charts of
  the glued scheme are compatible with the transitions of an arbitrary inclusion.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjGeneral.isPullback_transition_of_le_opens`: **Tag 01NO's
  cartesian square, for an arbitrary inclusion.**
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjGeneral.isOpenImmersion_transition_of_le_opens`: and the
  transition is an open immersion.

## The route

Tag 01N2 for a *basic* open inclusion is already available, because `Γ(D(f), 𝒜)` is a
localization of `Γ(U, 𝒜)` away from a degree-zero element. For `U ⊆ V` arbitrary, pick a section
`f` over `V` whose basic open `W` lies inside `U`. Then `W` is a basic open of `V` *and* of `U`,
so `Γ(W, 𝒜)` is a localization of `Γ(V, 𝒜)` and also of `Γ(U, 𝒜)`. A homogeneous `b` of degree
`d` over `U`, pushed into `W`, becomes the image of a homogeneous element of the same degree `d`
over `V` after multiplication by a power of the degree-zero element — this is
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProj.exists_mem_graded_mul_pow` — and the kernel of the second
localization lets that equality be cleared back to `Γ(U, 𝒜)` at the cost of a further power.

So `b` times a power of the image of each such section lies in the ideal generated by the
restrictions of the positive-degree homogeneous elements of `Γ(V, 𝒜)`. Those sections generate
the unit ideal of `Γ(S, U)`, because the basic opens of the affine open `V` form a basis of its
topology; collecting the exponents into a radical and using that the radical of the whole ring is
the whole ring gives `b` itself. No quasi-compactness argument and no partition of unity is
written by hand: the radical does that bookkeeping.

With Mathlib's hypothesis in hand, `GradedAlgebra.transition_eq_map` and
`GradedAlgebra.transition_comp` apply verbatim, which is Tag 01NP. The chart compatibility is
then checked on the open cover of `Proj Γ(U, 𝒜)` by the charts of the basic opens of `V` inside
`U`, where both legs are transitions along basic open inclusions and the compatibility is the
defining equation of the colimit. Finally the cartesian square is *not* proved by exhibiting the
transition as an open immersion with a computed image: it is obtained by cancelling the cartesian
square of the chart of `V` out of the cartesian square of the chart of `U`, both of which are
already stated for every affine open. Being an open immersion then follows from the square rather
than the reverse.

## Transparency notes

* `(U.basicOpen f).toOpens` and `S.basicOpen f` are equal by `rfl` but not at `implicit`
  transparency. A proof of the second placed where a proof of the first is expected makes the
  surrounding goal ill-typed at that transparency level, and `rw` then refuses to fire on it even
  though the term elaborated. Every inclusion proof fed to a transition below is therefore
  introduced by a `have` with the `toOpens` spelling ascribed, and the `S.basicOpen_le` form is
  used only in positions checked by `isDefEq`.
* For the same reason the inclusion `W.toOpens ≤ V.toOpens` cannot be packaged as a local `have`
  inside the proof of the key local step, since the rewrite by `GradedAlgebra.res_comp` has to
  match `𝒜.res (hWU.trans h)` syntactically; the chart `W` is instead a universally quantified
  site object and the two presentations of it enter as equational hypotheses.
* `GradedRingHom.map_mem` states membership through the `RingHom` coercion while `map_mul`
  produces the `FunLike` coercion of the graded hom itself. The two are definitionally equal but
  not syntactically, so the rewrite chain producing the localization equality is closed by `rfl`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 01N2](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01N2)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01NO](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01NO)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01NP](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01NP)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01NQ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01NQ)

## Not done here

The comparison isomorphisms on the twisting sheaves `𝒪(n)` are not constructed, so the two twist
clauses of Tag 01NO — that the canonical maps on the twists are isomorphisms, and that they are
compatible with multiplication — remain open, as does the relative `𝒪(n)` of Tag 01NP. Nothing is
said about quasi-compactness, separatedness or properness of the structure morphism, nor about a
graded algebra generated in degree one. The composition law of Tag 01NP is the only assertion
attached to a declaration here, on `transition_comp_of_le_opens`; the twist half of that tag and
Tags 01N2, 01NO and 01NQ carry no attribute in this file.
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits HomogeneousIdeal
open TopologicalSpace Opposite
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjShared Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProj
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjGlue

namespace Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjGeneral

universe u

section Base

variable {S : Scheme.{u}}

/-- Restricting a section of the bigger open does not change its basic open, provided that basic
open is already contained in the smaller one. -/
public theorem basicOpen_res_of_le {U V : S.Opens} (h : U ≤ V) (f : Γ(S, V))
    (hf : S.basicOpen f ≤ U) :
    S.basicOpen (S.presheaf.map (homOfLE h).op f) = S.basicOpen f :=
  (S.basicOpen_res f (homOfLE h).op).trans (inf_eq_right.mpr hf)

/-- The restrictions to `U` of the sections of `V` whose basic open is contained in `U` generate
the unit ideal of `Γ(S, U)`: their basic opens cover `U`, because the basic opens of the affine
open `V` form a basis of its topology. -/
public theorem span_res_sections_eq_top {U V : S.AffineZariskiSite}
    (h : U.toOpens ≤ V.toOpens) :
    Ideal.span {g : Γ(S, U.toOpens) | ∃ f : Γ(S, V.toOpens), S.basicOpen f ≤ U.toOpens ∧
      S.presheaf.map (homOfLE h).op f = g} = ⊤ := by
  rw [← U.2.self_le_iSup_basicOpen_iff]
  intro x hx
  obtain ⟨f, hfU, hxf⟩ := V.2.exists_basicOpen_le (V := U.toOpens) ⟨x, hx⟩ (h hx)
  refine TopologicalSpace.Opens.mem_iSup.mpr ⟨⟨_, ⟨f, hfU, rfl⟩⟩, ?_⟩
  rw [basicOpen_res_of_le h f hfU]
  exact hxf

end Base

section Relative

variable {S : Scheme.{u}} (𝒜 : GradedAlgebra S)

/-- Quasi-coherence read at an affine open presented as a basic open: if `W` *is* the basic open
of `f` in `U`, then the sections over `W` are the localization of the sections over `U` away from
the image of `f`. -/
public theorem isLocalization_res_of_eq {U W : S.AffineZariskiSite} (f : Γ(S, U.toOpens))
    (hW : W = U.basicOpen f) (hWU : W.toOpens ≤ U.toOpens) :
    letI : Algebra (𝒜.ring U) (𝒜.ring W) := 𝒜.algebra hWU
    IsLocalization.Away (𝒜.str U f) (𝒜.ring W) := by
  subst hW
  exact 𝒜.isLocalization U f

/-- **The local step of Tag 01N2 for an arbitrary inclusion.** Let `U ⊆ V` be affine opens and let
`W` be an affine open which is simultaneously the basic open of a section `f` over `V` and of a
section `g` over `U`, the two sections being compatible with the structure morphisms. Then a
homogeneous element `b` of degree `d` over `U`, multiplied by a power of the image of `g`, is a
multiple of the restriction of a homogeneous element of the *same* degree `d` over `V`.

The sections over `W` are a localization of the sections over `V` and also of the sections over
`U`. Pushing `b` into `W` and applying
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProj.exists_mem_graded_mul_pow` to the first presentation
produces the degree-`d` element over `V`; clearing the resulting equality back to `U` through the
second presentation produces the power. -/
public theorem exists_pow_mul_eq_res {U V W : S.AffineZariskiSite} (h : U.toOpens ≤ V.toOpens)
    (hWU : W.toOpens ≤ U.toOpens) (f : Γ(S, V.toOpens)) (g : Γ(S, U.toOpens))
    (hWf : W = V.basicOpen f) (hWg : W = U.basicOpen g)
    (hg : 𝒜.str U g = 𝒜.res h (𝒜.str V f))
    {d : ℕ} {b : 𝒜.ring U} (hb : b ∈ 𝒜.grading U d) :
    ∃ (N : ℕ) (c : 𝒜.ring U) (a : 𝒜.ring V), a ∈ 𝒜.grading V d ∧
      b * 𝒜.str U g ^ N = c * 𝒜.res h a := by
  let := 𝒜.algebra hWU
  let := 𝒜.algebra (hWU.trans h)
  have : IsLocalization.Away (𝒜.str U g) (𝒜.ring W) := isLocalization_res_of_eq 𝒜 g hWg hWU
  have : IsLocalization.Away (𝒜.str V f) (𝒜.ring W) :=
    isLocalization_res_of_eq 𝒜 f hWf (hWU.trans h)
  obtain ⟨a, k, ha, hak⟩ := exists_mem_graded_mul_pow (𝒜.grading V) (𝒜.grading W)
    (𝒜.res (hWU.trans h)) (𝒜.str_mem V f) (𝒜.algebraMap_eq (hWU.trans h))
    ((𝒜.res hWU).map_mem hb)
  have hcomp (x : 𝒜.ring V) : 𝒜.res (hWU.trans h) x = 𝒜.res hWU (𝒜.res h x) := by
    rw [𝒜.res_comp hWU h]; rfl
  have hstr : 𝒜.res (hWU.trans h) (𝒜.str V f) = 𝒜.res hWU (𝒜.str U g) := by
    rw [hg, hcomp]
  have hmap : ∀ x : 𝒜.ring U, algebraMap (𝒜.ring U) (𝒜.ring W) x = 𝒜.res hWU x := fun x =>
    congrArg (fun φ : 𝒜.ring U →+* 𝒜.ring W => φ x) (𝒜.algebraMap_eq hWU)
  have key : algebraMap (𝒜.ring U) (𝒜.ring W) (𝒜.res h a) =
      algebraMap (𝒜.ring U) (𝒜.ring W) (b * 𝒜.str U g ^ k) := by
    rw [hmap, hmap, map_mul, map_pow, ← hstr, ← hcomp, hak]
    rfl
  obtain ⟨⟨c, m, rfl⟩, hc⟩ := IsLocalization.exists_of_eq (M := Submonoid.powers (𝒜.str U g)) key
  exact ⟨m + k, 𝒜.str U g ^ m, a, ha, by linear_combination -hc⟩

/-- **Tag 01N2 for an arbitrary inclusion of affine opens.** Mathlib's hypothesis for
`AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.map` holds for the restriction map of a quasi-coherent graded algebra
along an arbitrary inclusion of affine opens, not only along a basic open inclusion.

The sections `x` over `U` with `b * str x` in the ideal generated by the restrictions of the
positive-degree homogeneous elements over `V` form an ideal of `Γ(S, U)`; the previous lemma says
it contains a power of every section coming from `V` whose basic open lies in `U`, and those
sections generate the unit ideal, so the ideal is the whole of `Γ(S, U)`. -/
public theorem irrelevant_le_map_res_of_le_opens {U V : S.AffineZariskiSite}
    (h : U.toOpens ≤ V.toOpens) :
    irrelevant (𝒜.grading U) ≤ (irrelevant (𝒜.grading V)).map (𝒜.res h) := by
  refine irrelevant_le_map_of_mem_span (𝒜.grading V) (𝒜.grading U) (𝒜.res h) fun d hd b hb => ?_
  set I := Ideal.span ((𝒜.res h) '' ⋃ n > 0, ((𝒜.grading V n : Set (𝒜.ring V))))
  let Q : Ideal Γ(S, U.toOpens) :=
    { carrier := {x | b * 𝒜.str U x ∈ I}
      add_mem' := fun {x y} hx hy => by
        change b * 𝒜.str U (x + y) ∈ I
        rw [map_add, mul_add]
        exact I.add_mem hx hy
      zero_mem' := by
        change b * 𝒜.str U 0 ∈ I
        rw [map_zero, mul_zero]
        exact I.zero_mem
      smul_mem' := fun c x hx => by
        change b * 𝒜.str U (c • x) ∈ I
        have h2 : b * 𝒜.str U (c • x) = 𝒜.str U c * (b * 𝒜.str U x) := by
          rw [smul_eq_mul, map_mul]; ring
        rw [h2]
        exact I.mul_mem_left _ hx }
  have hQ : Q = ⊤ := by
    refine Ideal.radical_eq_top.mp (top_le_iff.mp ?_)
    rw [← span_res_sections_eq_top (S := S) h, Ideal.span_le]
    rintro g ⟨f, hfU, rfl⟩
    obtain ⟨N, c, a, ha, heq⟩ := exists_pow_mul_eq_res 𝒜 h
      (W := U.basicOpen (S.presheaf.map (homOfLE h).op f)) (S.basicOpen_le _) f _
      (Subtype.ext (basicOpen_res_of_le h f hfU)) rfl (𝒜.res_str h f).symm hb
    refine ⟨N, ?_⟩
    change b * 𝒜.str U (S.presheaf.map (homOfLE h).op f ^ N) ∈ I
    rw [map_pow, heq]
    exact I.mul_mem_left c (Ideal.subset_span
      ⟨a, Set.mem_iUnion.mpr ⟨d, Set.mem_iUnion.mpr ⟨hd, ha⟩⟩, rfl⟩)
  have h1 : (1 : Γ(S, U.toOpens)) ∈ Q := hQ ▸ Submodule.mem_top
  have h2 : b * 𝒜.str U (1 : Γ(S, U.toOpens)) ∈ I := h1
  rwa [map_one, mul_one] at h2

/-- **Tag 01NO, the everywhere-defined morphism, for an arbitrary inclusion of affine opens.** -/
public theorem mapDomain_res_eq_top_of_le_opens {U V : S.AffineZariskiSite}
    (h : U.toOpens ≤ V.toOpens) :
    mapDomain (𝒜.grading V) (𝒜.grading U) (𝒜.res h) = ⊤ :=
  mapDomain_eq_top_of_irrelevant_le_map _ _ _ (irrelevant_le_map_res_of_le_opens 𝒜 h)

/-- The transition morphism of an arbitrary inclusion of affine opens is Mathlib's
`AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.map`. -/
public theorem transition_eq_map_of_le_opens {U V : S.AffineZariskiSite}
    (h : U.toOpens ≤ V.toOpens)
    (hdom : mapDomain (𝒜.grading V) (𝒜.grading U) (𝒜.res h) = ⊤) :
    𝒜.transition h hdom = Proj.map (𝒜.res h) (irrelevant_le_map_res_of_le_opens 𝒜 h) :=
  𝒜.transition_eq_map h hdom _

/-- **Tag 01NP for arbitrary inclusions of affine opens.** The transition morphisms compose: for
affine opens `U ⊆ V ⊆ W` of the base, the transition of `U ⊆ V` followed by the transition of
`V ⊆ W` is the transition of `U ⊆ W`. -/
public theorem transition_comp_of_le_opens {U V W : S.AffineZariskiSite}
    (hUV : U.toOpens ≤ V.toOpens) (hVW : V.toOpens ≤ W.toOpens)
    (hUVdom : mapDomain (𝒜.grading V) (𝒜.grading U) (𝒜.res hUV) = ⊤)
    (hVWdom : mapDomain (𝒜.grading W) (𝒜.grading V) (𝒜.res hVW) = ⊤)
    (hUWdom : mapDomain (𝒜.grading W) (𝒜.grading U) (𝒜.res (hUV.trans hVW)) = ⊤) :
    𝒜.transition hUV hUVdom ≫ 𝒜.transition hVW hVWdom = 𝒜.transition (hUV.trans hVW) hUWdom :=
  𝒜.transition_comp hUV hVW (irrelevant_le_map_res_of_le_opens 𝒜 hUV)
    (irrelevant_le_map_res_of_le_opens 𝒜 hVW) hUVdom hVWdom hUWdom

/-- **The charts are compatible with the transitions, for an arbitrary inclusion of affine
opens.**

Checked on the open cover of `Proj Γ(U, 𝒜)` by the charts of the basic opens of `V` contained in
`U`: such a chart maps to `Proj Γ(U, 𝒜)` and to `Proj Γ(V, 𝒜)` by transitions along *basic open*
inclusions, for which the compatibility is the defining equation of the glued scheme. -/
public theorem transition_comp_chart_of_le_opens {U V : S.AffineZariskiSite}
    (h : U.toOpens ≤ V.toOpens)
    (hdom : mapDomain (𝒜.grading V) (𝒜.grading U) (𝒜.res h) = ⊤) :
    𝒜.transition h hdom ≫ chart 𝒜 V = chart 𝒜 U := by
  refine (Scheme.Cover.mkOfCovers
    {f : Γ(S, V.toOpens) // S.basicOpen f ≤ U.toOpens}
    (fun i => 𝒜.projOver (U.basicOpen (S.presheaf.map (homOfLE h).op i.1)))
    (fun i => 𝒜.resMap U (S.presheaf.map (homOfLE h).op i.1))
    (fun y => by
      obtain ⟨f, hfU, hxf⟩ := V.2.exists_basicOpen_le (V := U.toOpens) (𝒜.toOpen U y)
        (h (𝒜.toOpen U y).2)
      have hy : y ∈ (𝒜.resMap U (S.presheaf.map (homOfLE h).op f)).opensRange := by
        rw [opensRange_resMap, basicOpen_res_of_le h f hfU]
        change 𝒜.toBase U y ∈ S.basicOpen f
        rw [← 𝒜.toOpen_ι U, Scheme.Hom.comp_apply]
        exact hxf
      obtain ⟨z, hz⟩ := hy
      exact ⟨⟨f, hfU⟩, z, hz⟩)).hom_ext _ _ fun i => ?_
  obtain ⟨f, hfU⟩ := i
  set g := S.presheaf.map (homOfLE h).op f
  have hWU : (U.basicOpen g).toOpens ≤ U.toOpens := S.basicOpen_le g
  have hle : U.basicOpen g ≤ V := ⟨f, (basicOpen_res_of_le h f hfU).symm⟩
  have htc : 𝒜.resMap U g ≫ 𝒜.transition h hdom =
      𝒜.transition (hWU.trans h) (mapDomain_res_eq_top_of_le_opens 𝒜 (hWU.trans h)) :=
    𝒜.transition_comp hWU h (𝒜.irrelevant_le_map_res U g)
      (irrelevant_le_map_res_of_le_opens 𝒜 h) _ _ _
  have hR : 𝒜.resMap U g ≫ chart 𝒜 U = chart 𝒜 (U.basicOpen g) :=
    transition_comp_chart 𝒜 (homOfLE (U.basicOpen_le g))
  change 𝒜.resMap U g ≫ 𝒜.transition h hdom ≫ chart 𝒜 V = 𝒜.resMap U g ≫ chart 𝒜 U
  rw [← Category.assoc, htc, hR]
  exact transition_comp_chart 𝒜 (homOfLE hle)

/-- **Tag 01NO: the square of a nested pair of affine opens is cartesian, for an arbitrary
inclusion.**

Obtained by cancelling the cartesian square of the chart of `V` out of the cartesian square of
the chart of `U`: both are instances of
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjGlue.isPullback_chart`, which is already stated for every
affine open, and the two paste together along the previous lemma. -/
public theorem isPullback_transition_of_le_opens {U V : S.AffineZariskiSite}
    (h : U.toOpens ≤ V.toOpens)
    (hdom : mapDomain (𝒜.grading V) (𝒜.grading U) (𝒜.res h) = ⊤) :
    IsPullback (𝒜.transition h hdom) (𝒜.toOpen U) (𝒜.toOpen V) (S.homOfLE h) := by
  refine IsPullback.of_right (h₁₂ := chart 𝒜 V) ?_ (𝒜.transition_toOpen h hdom)
    (isPullback_chart 𝒜 V).flip
  rw [transition_comp_chart_of_le_opens 𝒜 h hdom, Scheme.homOfLE_ι]
  exact (isPullback_chart 𝒜 U).flip

/-- The transition morphism of an arbitrary inclusion of affine opens is an open immersion, being
the base change of the inclusion of the affine opens. -/
public theorem isOpenImmersion_transition_of_le_opens {U V : S.AffineZariskiSite}
    (h : U.toOpens ≤ V.toOpens)
    (hdom : mapDomain (𝒜.grading V) (𝒜.grading U) (𝒜.res h) = ⊤) :
    IsOpenImmersion (𝒜.transition h hdom) :=
  MorphismProperty.of_isPullback (P := @IsOpenImmersion)
    (isPullback_transition_of_le_opens 𝒜 h hdom).flip inferInstance

end Relative

end Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjGeneral

end
